  "notes": [
    "AHM 560 Appendix I, printed page 74 — the CARGO LOADING INDEX TABLE on the LOAD AND TRIM SHEET plate (valid for MSNs 0810 and 0815). Rows are total main + lower load per loading zone in 500 kg brackets; values are whole index units.",
    "Reference only — never an input to a calculation. wnb-core computes each position's index exactly from positions.json's indexPerKg; this table is that same quantity rounded to whole index units over a 500 kg bracket.",
    "A blank cell means the plate greys that bracket out because it is above the zone's maximum load. The MAX row gives the index at the zone's maximum.",
    "Each column's slope tracks the corresponding main-deck position's indexPerKg to within 20% (13 of 17 zones within 10%). The four looser zones (F, H, J, K) are the near-neutral bays where index units are 0, 1 or 2 across the whole column, so integer rounding dominates the fit rather than any data disagreement.",
    "Transcribed from the operator's Cargo_Loading_Index_Table.xlsx (supplied 2026-09-09), then verified cell by cell against the approved AHM 560 PDF rendered at 600 dpi. Both agree, including the MAX row and every greyed-out cell. See AHM560_ERRATA.md Kayıt 8."
  ],
